I used to use the racket for all classes, so i know which characters
are suited to it and which are not. I also recently started to play
"go as fast as possible" and that means i started not using the
racket at all. Because of this, i have found that some classes which
are well suited for the racket are even better suited just to dive
and kill. 

Examples: A healer is the best racket character on the face of the
earth. Especially one that ends up with blessed !ofEH. If you are
good at the racket or pacifist it is the best choice. 

Valk The second best racket character. (especially a dwarf) the +3
shield is a great head start on armor and will have a good ac quick. 
If Con is high then they are a good candidate for modified racket.
(kill things up to level 3)  The drawback is that even for a good
racket/pacifist, it is even better just to use that long sword and
gain levels.  A lawful dwarf (which is better than a n valk at the 
racket) then can dip for excalibur when she hits lvl 5. 

Note, barb are not as easy as valks for the racket but basicly the
same applies to them.


Non Elven ranger- although their hp are not that great but because
they don't melee that well, this is also a good choice. Starting AC
stinks but the cloak of displacement helps you from taking damage as
long as you have room to dance. Just watch out for traps and
exploding doors. With those low hp being stunned can kill you. 

Again, because of the low hitpoints it would be better to do a
modified racket with this class. Unfortunately  the same benefits 
lends itself for dancing and using your bow to snipe monsters from a
distance. This removes some of the risk of traps instant killing you
as well as that pesky gnoll with the wand of MM getting off and
instant kill. Using your bow and diving are probably better then even
a modified racket on your chance for survival

 


